    {
      "id": "fb-005",
      "question": "How do tracking tokens work?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 25.51,
      "answer": "Tracking tokens in the NAVAS ecosystem are used to bill for GPS tracking based on time. Customers pay for tracking by the hour, day, or month, ensuring they only incur costs when assets are actively being tracked. This model supports the ability to pause and resume tracking as needed, allowing for flexible billing aligned with asset usage.\n\nSource: NAVAS Token Billing Strategy — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
